<a  href="/regionalization-evaluation-services"   class="c-card    c-card--arrow" >
        <div class="c-card__body">
                <div class="c-card__header">
                        <span class="c-card__title">
                                Animal Health Regionalization and Compartmentalization
                            </span>
        </div>
                    <div class="c-card__content">
                                 <p>APHIS evaluates the animal health statuses of foreign regions and compartments and the risk of disease introduction from imported commodities. This page includes information on how foreign regions can request an animal health status evaluation.</p>
            </div>
                                            <div class="c-card__footer">
                                    <span class="c-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            </div>
            </div>
        </a>

                </div>
                              <div class="grid-col-12 tablet:grid-col-6 c-card-grid__item" data-card-flag="">
                          


<a  href="/regionalization-evaluation-services/status-review"   class="c-card    c-card--arrow" >
        <div class="c-card__body">
                <div class="c-card__header">
                        <span class="c-card__title">
                                Animal Health Status Reviews
                            </span>
        </div>
                    <div class="c-card__content">
                                 <p>Our Regionalization Evaluation Services staff reviews the APHIS-recognized animal health statuses of foreign regions to ensure those regions continue to meet APHIS requirements for status. This page lists the regions and statuses reviewed or under review.</p>
            </div>
                                            <div class="c-card__footer">
                                    <span class="c-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            </div>
            </div>
        </a>

                </div>
            </div>
</div>

                      

